---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import AudienceBadge from "../components/AudienceBadge.astro";
import "../styles/how-it-works.css";
---

<Base
  title="How it works"
  active="how-it-works"
  section="system"
  description="A plain-language tour of the Podcast Factory: what goes in, the two choices made per book, the services it connects to, and how a book becomes a podcast — step by step."
>
  <div class="hiw-page">
    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         HERO
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div class="page-hero-inner">
        <span class="eyebrow">How it works</span>
        <h1 class="page-hero-title">A book goes in. A podcast comes out.</h1>
        <p class="page-hero-lede">
          No jargon on this page. This is the whole factory in plain language —
          what you drop in, the two choices it makes for every book, the outside
          services it leans on, and the exact journey from a scanned manuscript
          to a finished, verified podcast series. Two points along the way, it
          stops and waits for you.
        </p>
        <p class="home-hero-audience"><AudienceBadge tier="both" /></p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         SECTION 01 — MIND MAP
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="s01-mind-map" class="hiw-section">
      <h2><span class="num">01</span> The whole factory at a glance</h2>
      <p class="hiw-lead">
        One manuscript goes in. Before anything runs, two choices are set for
        that book — which kind of book edition to make, and which voice to
        record with. Then the factory calls on a handful of outside services and
        hands back several finished pieces.
      </p>

      <figure class="hiw-figure">
        {
          /* REQ-052: this is the one region on the page permitted to scroll, and
            a scrollable region has to be focusable or its right-hand half is
            mouse-only. Named after the diagram it holds. */
        }
        <div
          class="hiw-svg-scroll"
          role="region"
          aria-label="Podcast Factory mind map (scrolls sideways on narrow screens)"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          <svg
            class="hiw-svg"
            viewBox="0 0 960 560"
            role="img"
            aria-labelledby="mm-title mm-desc"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          >
            <title id="mm-title">Podcast Factory mind map</title>
            <desc id="mm-desc">
              A branching map. At the top, one book goes in. It fans into three
              branches: what you choose per book (book edition and audio voice,
              plus genre rules), what powers it (Microsoft Azure, Anthropic
              Claude, Google Gemini and NotebookLM, and an on-machine library),
              and what comes out (podcast episodes, two book editions, slide
              decks, and narrated video).
            </desc>

            <!-- Connectors root → branches -->
            <path class="mm-connector" d="M480 88 C 480 122 165 116 165 150"
            ></path>
            <path class="mm-connector" d="M480 88 L 480 150"></path>
            <path class="mm-connector" d="M480 88 C 480 122 795 116 795 150"
            ></path>
            <!-- Connectors branch → first leaf -->
            <path class="mm-connector" d="M165 204 L 165 232"></path>
            <path class="mm-connector" d="M480 204 L 480 232"></path>
            <path class="mm-connector" d="M795 204 L 795 232"></path>

            <!-- Root -->
            <rect class="n-root" x="310" y="24" width="340" height="64" rx="10"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-title"
              x="480"
              y="52"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="21">One scholarly book</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="480"
              y="73"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13">Arabic manuscript or written text</text
            >

            <!-- Branch A -->
            <rect
              class="n-branch branch-a"
              x="25"
              y="150"
              width="280"
              height="54"
              rx="8"></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-branch-title"
              x="165"
              y="176"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="15"
              ><tspan class="mm-num num-a">1 · </tspan>What you choose</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="165"
              y="194"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="12">set once, per book</text
            >
            <!-- Branch B -->
            <rect
              class="n-branch branch-b"
              x="340"
              y="150"
              width="280"
              height="54"
              rx="8"></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-branch-title"
              x="480"
              y="176"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="15"
              ><tspan class="mm-num num-b">2 · </tspan>What powers it</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="480"
              y="194"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="12">the services it calls</text
            >
            <!-- Branch C -->
            <rect
              class="n-branch branch-c"
              x="655"
              y="150"
              width="280"
              height="54"
              rx="8"></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-branch-title"
              x="795"
              y="176"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="15"
              ><tspan class="mm-num num-c">3 · </tspan>What comes out</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="795"
              y="194"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="12">the finished pieces</text
            >

            <!-- Leaves A -->
            <rect class="leaf-a" x="30" y="232" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="165"
              y="257"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Edition — translation or companion</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-a" x="30" y="292" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="165"
              y="317"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Audio — NotebookLM or auto-voice</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-a" x="30" y="352" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="165"
              y="377"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Genre rules per content type</text
            >

            <!-- Leaves B -->
            <rect class="leaf-b" x="345" y="232" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="480"
              y="257"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Microsoft Azure — read &amp; translate</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-b" x="345" y="292" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="480"
              y="317"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Anthropic Claude — write &amp; plan</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-b" x="345" y="352" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="480"
              y="377"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Google Gemini — slides &amp; video</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-b" x="345" y="412" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="480"
              y="437"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">NotebookLM — make the audio</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-b" x="345" y="472" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="480"
              y="497"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Local library — instant lookups</text
            >

            <!-- Leaves C -->
            <rect class="leaf-c" x="660" y="232" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="795"
              y="257"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Podcast episodes</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-c" x="660" y="292" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="795"
              y="317"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Two book editions (PDF)</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-c" x="660" y="352" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="795"
              y="377"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Slide decks</text
            >
            <rect class="leaf-c" x="660" y="412" width="270" height="48" rx="7"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="795"
              y="437"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13.5">Narrated video (optional)</text
            >
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          Every book sets two choices — a <strong>book edition</strong>
          (a faithful translation, or an augmented companion with editorial asides)
          and an <strong>audio voice</strong> (Google&rsquo;s NotebookLM, or a fully
          automated voice). Those two switches, plus the content&rsquo;s genre, are
          what make each series different.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         SECTION 02 — THE JOURNEY (timeline)
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="s02-journey" class="hiw-section">
      <h2><span class="num">02</span> A book&rsquo;s journey, step by step</h2>
      <p class="hiw-lead">
        From the moment you drop a book in to the moment it ships — eleven
        plain-language steps here (the factory runs about thirty under the
        hood). Everything runs on its own except the two amber steps, where it
        stops and waits for your approval.
      </p>

      <ol class="hiw-timeline">
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">1</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Drop in the book</h3>
            <p>
              Add a scholarly PDF (often scanned Arabic) or already-written
              text. From here on, it runs by itself until it asks for you.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">2</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Read the pages</h3>
            <p>
              It reads the scanned pages and, for Arabic sources, translates
              them into clean English to work from.
            </p>
            <span class="hiw-step-svc">Microsoft Azure — OCR + Translator</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">3</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Tidy the text</h3>
            <p>
              Removes scanning and printing noise — page numbers, headers,
              broken line-breaks — while protecting every word of the actual
              scholarship.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">4</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Learn the vocabulary</h3>
            <p>
              Builds a glossary of names and terms with correct pronunciations,
              so nothing important is mangled when it is spoken aloud.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step is-halt">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">5</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Plan the episodes</h3>
            <p>
              It decides the chapters, the angle, and the two hosts — then
              stops.
              <strong>You approve the plan.</strong> Nothing expensive is written
              until you say go.
            </p>
            <span class="hiw-halt-badge">✋ Waits for you</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">6</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Write each episode</h3>
            <p>
              Chapter by chapter, it drafts the narrator framing — the script
              that guides the conversation.
            </p>
            <span class="hiw-step-svc">Anthropic Claude</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">7</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Enrich &amp; verify</h3>
            <p>
              Adds citations from an on-machine library and checks names and
              references against trusted sources — at no extra cost.
            </p>
            <span class="hiw-step-svc">On-machine Source Library</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">8</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Quality review</h3>
            <p>
              Automated reviewers challenge every chapter for accuracy and
              voice, and loop fixes until it passes — 15 checks per book.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">9</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Make the slides</h3>
            <p>
              A matching slide deck is authored for each episode, for the visual
              version. (Optional, on by default.)
            </p>
            <span class="hiw-step-svc">Google Gemini</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step is-halt">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">10</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Assemble everything</h3>
            <p>
              It gathers the finished pieces and stops.
              <strong>You review and sign off.</strong> Nothing publishes without
              this.
            </p>
            <span class="hiw-halt-badge">✋ Waits for you</span>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="hiw-step">
          <div class="hiw-step-num">11</div>
          <div class="hiw-step-body">
            <h3>Produce &amp; deliver</h3>
            <p>
              NotebookLM (or the automated voice) records the audio; the book
              editions are composed as PDFs; and everything is copied to your
              Google Drive.
            </p>
            <span class="hiw-step-svc">NotebookLM · Google Drive</span>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         SECTION 03 — SERVICES & CONNECTIONS
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="s03-services" class="hiw-section">
      <h2><span class="num">03</span> The services it connects to</h2>
      <p class="hiw-lead">
        The factory runs on your machine but calls out to a few trusted services
        to do the heavy lifting. Here is the connection in one picture, then
        every service and exactly what it is for.
      </p>

      <figure class="hiw-figure">
        <div
          class="hiw-svg-scroll"
          role="region"
          aria-label="How the factory connects to outside services (scrolls sideways on narrow screens)"
          tabindex="0"
        >
          <svg
            class="hiw-svg"
            viewBox="0 0 960 210"
            role="img"
            aria-labelledby="conn-title conn-desc"
            xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
          >
            <title id="conn-title">
              How the factory connects to outside services
            </title>
            <desc id="conn-desc">
              Three boxes left to right. On the left, your machine holds the
              book. In the middle, cloud services (Azure, Claude, Gemini and
              NotebookLM) read, write and voice it. On the right, the finished
              files come back to your own Google Drive.
            </desc>

            <!-- Arrows -->
            <path
              class="mm-connector"
              d="M280 105 L 348 105"
              marker-end="url(#hiw-arrow)"></path>
            <path
              class="mm-connector"
              d="M612 105 L 680 105"
              marker-end="url(#hiw-arrow)"></path>
            <defs>
              <marker
                id="hiw-arrow"
                markerWidth="9"
                markerHeight="9"
                refX="7"
                refY="3"
                orient="auto"
                markerUnits="strokeWidth"
              >
                <path d="M0 0 L 7 3 L 0 6 z" fill="var(--c-ink-muted)"></path>
              </marker>
            </defs>

            <!-- Left: your machine -->
            <rect
              class="n-surface"
              x="30"
              y="60"
              width="250"
              height="90"
              rx="10"></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="155"
              y="98"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="15">Your machine</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="155"
              y="120"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13">holds the book &amp; the pipeline</text
            >

            <!-- Middle: cloud services -->
            <rect class="n-root" x="348" y="45" width="264" height="120" rx="10"
            ></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="480"
              y="80"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="15">Cloud services</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="480"
              y="104"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13">Azure reads &amp; translates</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="480"
              y="124"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13">Claude &amp; Gemini write &amp; plan</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="480"
              y="144"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13">NotebookLM voices it</text
            >

            <!-- Right: your drive -->
            <rect
              class="n-surface"
              x="680"
              y="60"
              width="250"
              height="90"
              rx="10"></rect>
            <text
              class="mm-label"
              x="805"
              y="98"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="15">Your Google Drive</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="805"
              y="120"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13">finished audio, books &amp; video</text
            >

            <!-- Arrow labels -->
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="314"
              y="96"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13">text out</text
            >
            <text
              class="mm-sub"
              x="646"
              y="96"
              text-anchor="middle"
              font-size="13">files back</text
            >
          </svg>
        </div>
        <figcaption>
          The book&rsquo;s text is the only thing that leaves your machine, and
          only so these services can read, write and voice it. Everything
          produced comes back to a Google Drive you control.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="hiw-provider-grid">
        <section class="hiw-provider prov-microsoft">
          <p class="hiw-provider-kicker">Reads the source</p>
          <h3 class="hiw-provider-name">Microsoft Azure</h3>
          <ul class="hiw-svc">
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">Document Intelligence</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-auto">Auto</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">Reads scanned Arabic pages (OCR).</div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">Translator</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-auto">Auto</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">Turns the Arabic into English.</div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">Speech</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-auto">Auto</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">
                Transcribes the finished audio so it can be checked.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="hiw-provider prov-anthropic">
          <p class="hiw-provider-kicker">Writes &amp; plans</p>
          <h3 class="hiw-provider-name">Anthropic</h3>
          <ul class="hiw-svc">
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">Claude</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-auto">Auto</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">
                The writing brain — refines the text, plans the episodes, drafts
                the narration, and composes the book editions.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="hiw-provider prov-google">
          <p class="hiw-provider-kicker">Produces &amp; delivers</p>
          <h3 class="hiw-provider-name">Google</h3>
          <ul class="hiw-svc">
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">Gemini</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-auto">Auto</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">
                Plans slide decks and video scenes, and runs an independent
                quality audit.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">NotebookLM</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-manual">Manual</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">
                Turns each script into a natural two-host audio conversation.
                You upload and download this by hand.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">Drive</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-auto">Auto</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">
                Receives the finished audio, books, and video.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="hiw-provider prov-other">
          <p class="hiw-provider-kicker">Voice &amp; knowledge</p>
          <h3 class="hiw-provider-name">Others</h3>
          <ul class="hiw-svc">
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">ElevenLabs</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-auto">Auto</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">
                An alternate, fully automated voice engine when NotebookLM
                isn&rsquo;t used.
              </div>
            </li>
            <li>
              <span class="hiw-svc-name">On-machine Source Library</span>
              <span class="hiw-tag tag-local">Local</span>
              <div class="hiw-svc-what">
                A local store of the Quran and twenty years of scholarship —
                instant lookups at zero cost, never leaving your machine.
              </div>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </section>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         CLOSING — deep-dive links
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="s04-technical" class="hiw-deepdive">
      <h2>Want the technical version?</h2>
      <p>
        This page is the plain-language tour. For the engineering detail — every
        station, the branch logic by content genre, the exact services and keys,
        and the design decisions — follow these.
      </p>
      <div class="hiw-deepdive-links">
        <a href="/architecture">Architecture</a>
        <a href="/pipeline-paths">Pipeline paths by category</a>
        <a href="/system-map">System map</a>
        <a href="/infrastructure">Infrastructure</a>
        <a href="/security">Security</a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
